    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s action with **Corbin Carroll** standing as the clear anchor of the lineup, boasting an elite 82.21 score. He benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against R. V\u00e1squez (4.80 xERA) and dynamic platoon splits, positioning him as our primary source of speed and power today. **Isaac Paredes** (67.49) and **Gabriel Moreno** (67.73) also present strong value; **Paredes** is bolstered by a park-factor boost and platoon advantage against Seth Johnson, while **Moreno** projects well despite the \"Lineup Pending\" tag. **Brice Turang** remains a tactical start at 64.81, specifically targeted for his theft potential against a slower-to-the-plate pitcher, reinforcing our organizational commitment to the scarcest category: stolen bases.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision was bypassing **Moises Ballesteros** (43.93), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Trevor Story** and **Cole Young**. While **Ballesteros** showed respectable efficiency, his matchup against Logan Gilbert (3.46 xERA) forced the optimizer to favor hitters with higher-ceiling matchups or more favorable platoon alignments. Risks remain elevated today due to the widespread \"Lineup Pending\" status across our roster; specifically, **Josh Naylor** (59.80) faces a tough individual test against Yusei Kikuchi, and **James Wood** (63.47) is navigating a challenging park environment. We are keeping a close eye on **Jose Caballero** as well; while his base projections are solid, the negative wind forecast and poor platoon splits necessitate a cautious outlook for his final output. We continue to keep **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Mickey Moniak** sidelined due to injury and lineup unavailability, respectively, alongside the bench-depth group of **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Max Muncy**, and **Edwin Arroyo** as we monitor late-game shifts.",
